[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114386,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Glandular odontogenic cyst (GOC) is a developmental cyst in which the epithelial lining resembles glandular tissue.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114387,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114388,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DA05.0 Developmental odontogenic cysts</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114389,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> sialo-odontogenic cyst; mucoepidermoid odontogenic cyst.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114390,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114391,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GOC arises in tooth-bearing areas of the jaws. About 75% of cases are in the mandible. Mandibular and maxillary lesions have a propensity for the anterior regions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114392,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GOC usually presents as a slowly expanding, painless swelling.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>GOCs are well-defined, corticated, unilocular or multilocular radiolucencies. Tooth displacement or root resorption is seen in as many as 25% of cases. Lesions may reach a large size and cross the midline in the mandible {12775659; 28744957}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114393,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GOCs account for &lt;&nbsp;0.5% of odontogenic cysts {16918602}. There is no sex predilection. The average age at presentation is about 50&nbsp;years, with a peak in the fifth to seventh decades of life {28744957}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114394,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114395,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "<p >GOC is a developmental cyst thought to arise from cell rests of the dental lamina. No pathogenic variants were detected in a panel of 50&nbsp;oncogenes and tumour suppressor genes screened by next-generation sequencing {28866361}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T16:52:31"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114396,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GOCs are often multicystic or lobular. The cyst wall may have thickenings or papillary projections.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114397,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GOCs are often multilocular cysts and are lined by epithelium of variable thickness, from a thin layer of flattened squamous or cuboidal cells to stratified squamous epithelium, often with whorled epithelial thickenings, or plaques similar to those in lateral periodontal cyst. Cuboidal or low columnar cells on the luminal surface (hobnail cells) are found in all cases. Other typical features include intraepithelial microcysts, apocrine metaplasia, clear cells, papillary projections (tufting), cilia, and mucous cells {16043383; 21915706; 28744957}. Not all features are present in every case, and a higher number of features allows more confident diagnosis {21915706}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>GOC may show similar features to central mucoepidermoid carcinoma and this must be considered in the differential diagnosis {21915706; 18248589}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114398,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114399,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GOC is generally considered to be negative for <em>MAML2</em> gene rearrangements {24647913}. However, recent studies have shown rearrangements in lesions that meet the histological criteria for GOC. These lesions may have been central mucoepidermoid carcinoma at the outset, but it raises the possibility that some central mucoepidermoid carcinomas might develop from a pre-existing GOC, and <em>MAML2</em> rearrangement studies must be interpreted with caution {29121421}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114400,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a radiolucent cystic lesion in a tooth-bearing area of the jaw; often multilocular.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> a lining of variable thickness with epithelial thickenings, plaques, or papillary projections; luminal columnar or cuboidal (hobnail) cells; microcysts or duct-like structures; mucous or clear cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114401,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114402,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 129,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GOCs, especially large and multilocular lesions, recur after enucleation in about 22% of cases {15789313; 28744957}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-03T15:05:20"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]